2. THE WINDOW'S EDGES, from record l9t5's T10 output (v2/docs/records/l9t5/l9t5_t10.out, parsed; line numbers of that file), revision V (fitted, L9T5-D7), 14.0k
   the corner: inside air 76.25 C (line 100); the pre-regulator 3.9063 to 4.1174 V, the LDO's least output 3.2505 V, so its drop 0.8669 V and
     159.5 K/A on the AP2112K's 184 C/W (line 531; PRINTED, no heat sink, DS39724 p.3); criterion 125 C for every sustained state (SESSION,
     the owner's part 22), 150 C the absolute maximum, never an operating target
   UPPER EDGE, the LDO's 125 C current at the corner, I125 = (125 - 76.25) / (theta x 0.8669 V) (MODEL on PRINTED theta):
     SOT25 (AP2112K)      theta 184.0 C/W  I125 0.3056 A
     SO-8 (AP2112M)       theta 114.0 C/W  I125 0.4933 A
     SOT89-5 (AP2112R5)   theta 120.0 C/W  I125 0.4686 A
     (the three are DS39724's own rows, p.3, 'No Heatsink'; the board is not printed: realising any of them on board B's copper is a
     Layer 10 means, as T10 already says of the 184 C/W)
   LOWER EDGES, the currents the design must serve (each regulator's total: controller, auxiliaries, both transceivers):
     S1 the largest SUSTAINED served state (an average over FW-B21's window): 0.1855 A, line 653 (MODEL; 'a babbler, the limiters bounding it')
     S2 the normal-service PEAK, both transceivers dominant at once (a frame on each fabric): 0.2839 A, line 546 (MODEL: 10i's
        babbling row has exactly this composition, the bounded controller, the circuit's auxiliaries and both transceivers at the
        60 mA dominant row, PRINTED; in normal traffic it lasts bit times, not a sustained state)
     S3 IOHA row 7's fault rows, held (the faulted transceiver dominant into the fault, the other at its share), rev V (10e):
        B1   0.3486 A, line 392
        B2   0.3486 A, line 393
        B3   0.2495 A, line 394
        B4   0.2846 A, line 395
        B5   0.3686 A, line 396
        B6   0.2236 A, line 397
        B7a  0.2286 A, line 398
        B7b  0.2286 A, line 399
        and the brief's (f1) 0.3726 A (line 191; round 4's controller figure, rev Y at 144 MHz: a cover, larger than rev V's B1)
     S3' the same rows with the healthy fabric's transceiver dominant in the same bit (MODEL: held - 0.0046 A share + 0.060 A dominant):
        B1   0.4040 A
