3. THE CANDIDATES: integrated current-limited switches with a PRINTED limit near 0.2 to 0.6 A and a PRINTED fault timer with latch-off
   C1 TI SLVS841F (TPS2552, TPS2553, TPS2552-1, TPS2553-1; November 2008, revised August 2016)
      TPS2553-1 (latch-off, active-high EN; TPS2552-1 the active-low twin), SOT-23-6 (DBV) or WSON-6 (DRV); VIN 2.5 to 6.5 V (7.3)
      IOS PRINTED rows (7.5, p.7): RILIM 49.9 kOhm, -40 C <= TJ <= 125 C: 0.475 / 0.520 / 0.565 A; RILIM 210 kOhm: 0.110 / 0.130 / 0.150 A
      the maker's equations (9.5.1, p.15; include temperature and process, not the resistor): IOSmin = 25230 / R^1.016, IOSmax = 22980 / R^0.94 mA,
        R in kOhm, 15 to 232 kOhm
      rDS(on) DBV at most 0.135 ohm, -40 C <= TJ <= 125 C (p.7); RthJA DBV 182.6, DRV 72.0 C/W (7.4, p.6)
      FAULT TIMER: the overcurrent deglitch 5 / 7.5 / 10 ms (min / typ / max, PRINTED, p.7); LATCH-OFF: '...limits the current to
        IOS until the overload condition is removed or the internal deglitch time is reached and the device is latched off' (9.3.1,
        p.14); off 'until power is cycled or the device enable is toggled' (p.13); turnoff time at most 3 ms (p.7)
      NOT PRINTED: whether the deglitch restarts when an overload clears for a moment; the sheet says only 'The deglitch circuitry
        delays entering and leaving fault conditions' (9.3.3, p.14). The response is 2 us TYPICAL only
   C2 Diodes DS41186 Rev. 5 - 2 (AP22652, AP22653, AP22652A, AP22653A; March 2026)
      AP22653A (latch-off, active-high EN; AP22652A active-low), SOT26 or W-DFN2020-6; VIN 3.0 to 5.5 V
      ILIMIT PRINTED rows (p.5): RLIM 49.9 kOhm, -40 C <= TA <= +85 C: 0.441 / 0.490 / 0.539 A; RLIM 210 kOhm at TA 25 C only: 0.095 / 0.125 / 0.155 A
      the maker's best-fit equations (p.10; temperature and process, not the resistor): ILIMIT_Min = 28955 / R^1.075, ILIMIT_Max = 31033 / R^1.031 mA
      RDS(ON) SOT26 at most 0.135 ohm, -40 C <= TA <= +85 C (p.5); theta JA SOT26 120 C/W on a JEDEC high-K board (p.4)
      FAULT TIMER: tBLANK 2 / 6 / 20 ms (PRINTED, p.6); LATCH-OFF: the A versions are 'turned off' when 'the internal deglitch time
        (6ms typical) is reached' and 'remain latched off until power is cycled or the device enable is toggled' (p.9); that this
        deglitch is the tBLANK row is INFERRED (the row names the FAULT flag); its restart on a momentary clearing is NOT PRINTED
   considered and not taken:
      TI TPS2596 (SLVSET8A, in the tree): its latch-off variants latch only at thermal shutdown (TSD 157 C, p.7, a TYPICAL figure)
        and it 'exits current limiting when the load current falls below ILIM' (p.22): no printed fault timer
      TI TPS25200 (SLVSCJ0F): constant current until 'the device begins to thermal cycle' (p.12): no latch-off, a periodic waveform
      ADI MAX4995A: not read (section 1)

4. ROW 1: THE WINDOW AGAINST THE ROWS THE DESIGN MUST SERVE (IOHA row 7, line 244: 'quorum continues on the other fabric')
   W1, no served state limited: IOSmin >= the served peak and IOSmax <= I125. W2, served peaks limited and bridged by local capacitance:
   IOSmin >= S1, IOSmax <= I125, the bridging capacitance <= what the latch-off limiter can start into, AND a latch timer that restarts
   between limited intervals (printed by neither candidate: W2 can never be shown on printed limits)
   (a) M-A as registered: the limiter ahead of the AP2112K (SOT25, 184 C/W): I125 0.3056 A
     W1 against S2 alone needs IOSmax / IOSmin <= 0.3056 / 0.2839 = 1.077 (a +-3.7 % band); against S3' (0.4240 A) the edges cross: CLOSED
     C1 TPS2553-1: the highest band under I125 at an E96 resistor (1 %): 102.0 kOhm, IOS 0.2274 to 0.3002 A (ratio 1.320; MODEL on the maker's equations)
     C2 AP22653A: the highest band under I125 at an E96 resistor (1 %): 90.9 kOhm, IOS 0.2247 to 0.2999 A (ratio 1.335; MODEL on the maker's equations)
     so W1 is CLOSED at 184 C/W for both candidates: normal service (S2) and every row-7 fault above IOSmin would be limited
     W2, the capacitance (MODEL): a limited interval t at a peak I needs C = (I - IOSmin) x t / dV on the supervisor's 3.3 V rail, dV =
       the LDO's least output 3.2505 V less the TCAN334's least supply 3.0 V (PRINTED, SLLSEQ7F 5.3, p.5) = 0.2505 V; the latch-off limiter
       starts into at most C = (IOSmin - S1) x t_latch(min) / 3.3495 V (the rail charged at its least limit while the supervisor draws S1;
       the soft start not credited)
       intervals: a frame on record l9t5's frame model, 135 bit-times at 500 kbit/s (FW-B21's least rate) = 270 us (ASSUMPTION, T10's);
       a run of 11 successive dominant bits on TXD, TI's printed protocol worst case (SLLSEQ7F 5.7 note 1, p.9) = 22 us; a held TXD
       ended by the driver time-out, 3.8 ms (PRINTED maximum)
     C1 TPS2553-1 at 102.0 kOhm (IOSmin 0.2274 A, latch at least 5 ms): it can start into at most 62.5 uF
       S2 normal frames, both transceivers dominant   0.2839 A for   270.0 us: bridging   60.9 uF  fits
       B3 frames (the bus still works), S3'           0.3049 A for   270.0 us: bridging   83.5 uF  OVER the start limit
       B4 frames (the bus still works), S3'           0.3400 A for   270.0 us: bridging  121.4 uF  OVER the start limit
       B1/B2 error runs (bits read wrong), S3'        0.4040 A for    22.0 us: bridging   15.5 uF  fits
       B5 error runs (bits read wrong), S3'           0.4240 A for    22.0 us: bridging   17.3 uF  fits
       B7a a held TXD into the healthy bus, held      0.2286 A for  3800.0 us: bridging   18.2 uF  fits
     C2 AP22653A at 90.9 kOhm (IOSmin 0.2247 A, latch at least 2 ms): it can start into at most 23.4 uF
       S2 normal frames, both transceivers dominant   0.2839 A for   270.0 us: bridging   63.8 uF  OVER the start limit
       B3 frames (the bus still works), S3'           0.3049 A for   270.0 us: bridging   86.4 uF  OVER the start limit
       B4 frames (the bus still works), S3'           0.3400 A for   270.0 us: bridging  124.3 uF  OVER the start limit
       B1/B2 error runs (bits read wrong), S3'        0.4040 A for    22.0 us: bridging   15.7 uF  fits
       B5 error runs (bits read wrong), S3'           0.4240 A for    22.0 us: bridging   17.5 uF  fits
       B7a a held TXD into the healthy bus, held      0.2286 A for  3800.0 us: bridging   59.0 uF  OVER the start limit
     so on the record's own frame model W2 conflicts for both candidates (B4's limited frame needs more capacitance than the latch-off
     limiter can start into), and on any interval model it rests on a latch timer whose restart is not printed: M-A at 184 C/W has NO
     WINDOW ON PRINTED LIMITS for the rows the design must serve
   (b) THE THERMAL-HEADROOM COMPANION: the limit raised over every served peak, the LDO's junction-to-ambient lowered to hold it
     C1 TPS2553-1 at 49.9 kOhm: the PRINTED row 0.475 to 0.565 A with the resistor's 1 % through the exponents: IOS 0.4702 to 0.5704 A (MODEL);
       IOSmin over S3' by +0.0462 A, over S1 by +0.2847 A: W1 holds on the served side; the LDO must hold 125 C at 0.5704 A: theta at most 98.6 C/W
       (the tested row governs; the maker's design equation at 49.9 kOhm reads 0.4702 to 0.5878 A with the 1 %, theta at most 95.7 C/W if taken)
       SOT25 (AP2112K)      184.0 C/W: junction 167.2 C at 0.5704 A  FAILS
       SO-8 (AP2112M)       114.0 C/W: junction 132.6 C at 0.5704 A  FAILS
       SOT89-5 (AP2112R5)   120.0 C/W: junction 135.6 C at 0.5704 A  FAILS
     C2 AP22653A at 49.9 kOhm: the PRINTED row 0.441 to 0.539 A with the resistor's 1 % through the exponents: IOS 0.4363 to 0.5446 A (MODEL);
       IOSmin over S3' by +0.0123 A, over S1 by +0.2508 A: W1 holds on the served side; the LDO must hold 125 C at 0.5446 A: theta at most 103.3 C/W
       (the tested row governs; the maker's design equation at 49.9 kOhm reads 0.4282 to 0.5566 A with the 1 %, theta at most 101.0 C/W if taken)
       SOT25 (AP2112K)      184.0 C/W: junction 163.1 C at 0.5446 A  FAILS
       SO-8 (AP2112M)       114.0 C/W: junction 130.1 C at 0.5446 A  FAILS
       SOT89-5 (AP2112R5)   120.0 C/W: junction 132.9 C at 0.5446 A  FAILS
     so no AP2112 package holds the companion's maximum: the companion is a different regulator part with a PRINTED junction-to-ambient
     at most 98.6 C/W (C1) or 103.3 C/W (C2) at this corner, rated at least the limiter's maximum (section 8)
     no capacitance is needed to bridge a served frame (none is limited); the latch-off limiter starts into at most 425 uF (C1, 5 ms)
     or 150 uF (C2, 2 ms) on the rail, the decoupling's ceiling (MODEL)
     row 8 (S4, survive only): (f2) 0.5491 A and rev V's 0.5639 A against IOS 0.4702 to 0.5704 A: may be limited (no service is owed; IOHA
       line 245: 'no controller can form a majority; firmware rule is that a controller without quorum does not act, so the voters hold the home assignment');
       a limiter that latches leaves its supervisor off until EN or power is cycled: the home assignment holds either way; the
       recovery after the repair is a restart (the peers' EN, section 6)
     what the companion gives up: its IOSmin (0.4702 A) is over the H743's own 125 C current 0.328 A (line 101), so a firmware fault outside
       FW-B20 can still take the controller past its rating (T10 10h (3): a systematic firmware defect, not a protective mechanism); M-A
       at 184 C/W (IOSmax 0.3002 A) would have held it, had it a window; HO-E (VOS0 from 0.1936 A) is under every IOSmin either way (L4A-59)

5. ROW 2: THE LDO OUTPUT SHORT (AP2112 'foldback short current 50 mA (TYPICAL)', T10 line 144; 'acts in no row', line 210)
   (i) the short draws the limiter's own limit through the LDO (the LDO fully on): the limiter limits and latches off within its
       PRINTED timer: the event's energy
       at most 4.1174 V x 0.5704 A x 10 ms = 23.5 mJ (C1 companion) or 44.8 mJ (C2, 20 ms); with M-A at 184 C/W, 12.4 mJ (C1 at 102.0 kOhm)
       (MODEL, the whole input across whichever part holds the drop); BOUNDED on printed limits
   (ii) the LDO holds its own short current under the limiter's limit (the AP2112's foldback 50 mA is TYPICAL, no maximum printed; a
       companion part's own limit and foldback are likewise its own): the limiter does not act; the LDO holds the
       whole input at its own short current for as long as the short lasts (0.206 W at the typical, 114.1 C at 184 C/W: a TYPICAL reading,
       never a bound). EXCLUDED from the LDO-junction criterion, with the reason (SESSION): a supervisor on a shorted rail is already
       lost, which IOHA row 3 (line 240) carries: 'the other two are a majority and ownership is unaffected'; the containment that row needs is held on PRINTED
       limits whatever the LDO does: +5V_IOC and the other two branches see at most IOSmax from it, and an LDO that fails shorted
       input to output becomes case (i), which latches. The bounded-interval disconnection of a dead branch is the peers' vote on its
       limiter's EN (L4A-54's M-B vote outputs; turnoff at most 3 ms PRINTED): a finding for L4A-54 and L4A-56, not a printed timer
   result: a PRINTED fault timer with latch-off on both candidates (C1 5 to 10 ms, C2 2 to 20 ms); the sub-case under the
   limit is excluded with its reason, not bounded

6. ROW 3: THE LIMITER'S OWN DISSIPATION WHILE LIMITING, AND ITS RESTART WAVEFORM
   C1 TPS2553-1 companion: in service at S3' 0.4240 A, 24.3 mW (rDS(on) 0.135 ohm PRINTED): junction 80.7 C at 182.6 C/W (MODEL); limiting into a
     shorted output at most 4.1174 V x 0.5704 A = 2.348 W for at most 10 ms (the timer's PRINTED maximum), 23.5 mJ; its junction in that
     time is NOT computed (no transient thermal impedance printed): surviving it is the part's stated function (both sheets: short
     circuits), backed by its own thermal protection
   C2 AP22653A companion: in service at S3' 0.4240 A, 24.3 mW (rDS(on) 0.135 ohm PRINTED): junction 79.2 C at 120.0 C/W (MODEL); limiting into a
     shorted output at most 4.1174 V x 0.5446 A = 2.242 W for at most 20 ms (the timer's PRINTED maximum), 44.8 mJ; its junction in that
     time is NOT computed (no transient thermal impedance printed): surviving it is the part's stated function (both sheets: short
     circuits), backed by its own thermal protection
   C1's thermal sensor in current limit acts from 135 C (minimum, 9.3.6, p.14); C2's at approximately 145 C (p.10, no limit printed)
   RESTART: the latch-off versions do not restart by themselves (C1 p.13, C2 p.9): no periodic waveform of their own. Two exceptions:
     a hard short at the limiter's own output may thermal-cycle it inside the timer (whether the deglitch completes across a thermal
     cycle is NOT PRINTED): a periodic waveform in the limiter alone, its current at most IOSmax (PRINTED), so the containment holds and
     the LDO is not in that path; and a restart the peers command through EN (L4A-54, L4A-58) must bound its own rate: at most one
     attempt per T_r keeps the average at most 23.5 mJ / T_r (2.3 mW at 10 s)
   the reverse-voltage latch (C1: VOUT - VIN 95 to 190 mV held 3 to 7 ms, PRINTED, p.7) needs the LDO's input capacitance to
     stay above a falling +5V_IOC for 3 ms against the supervisor's own draw (10 uF at 10 mA falls 1 V a ms): not a credible trip in
     service (MODEL); at power-down it latches nothing that a power cycle does not clear

7. ROW 4: T10-A3'S HEADROOM WITH THE LIMITER'S RESISTANCE IN PLACE OF THE 0.3 OHM SENSE (the supply path exactly as T10 computes it:
   the pre-regulator's least 3.9063 V, the rail's 2 % budget, the lead and contacts 0.04252 ohm at the total current, the return's shift 0.0681 V)
   reproduced first: at 0.2452 A with 0.3 ohm at +1 %: 3.6524 V against 3.5213 V (T10 line 643 prints 3.6524 against 3.5213): EQUAL
   (a) C1 TPS2553-1's 0.135 ohm at T10's point, 0.2452 A on all three: 3.6936 V against 3.5213 V: +0.1723 V, holds
   (a) C2 AP22653A's 0.135 ohm at T10's point, 0.2452 A on all three: 3.6936 V against 3.5213 V: +0.1723 V, holds
   (b) at each design's largest sustained current, IOSmax on all three (the AP2112's dropout rows, INFERRED between 300 and 600 mA as T10):
       M-A at 184 C/W, C1 at 102.0 kOhm   0.3002 A: 3.6791 V against 3.5595 V: +0.1196 V, holds
       companion, C1 at 49.9 kOhm         0.5704 A: 3.6082 V against 3.7486 V: -0.1404 V, FAILS on the AP2112's rows
       so the companion regulator's PRINTED dropout at 0.5704 A must be at most 3.6082 - 3.3683 = 0.2399 V (with the AP2112's output band and
       load regulation; its own rows replace them)
   (c) the other two while one sits at the companion's IOSmax: lead 0.9414 A, each other LDO at S1 0.1855 A: 3.6929 V against 3.4798 V: +0.2131 V, holds
   (d) the connected path upstream: three limiters at their maximum draw 1.7111 A from U601 and the lead's pin 1, against U601's 3 A and
       the VH's 10 A (PRINTED, T10 line 272): holds; a shorted branch takes at most IOSmax from them, so the other two keep their supply
   (e) S3' on all three in one bit (error flags overlap): 3.6466 V against 3.6462 V on the AP2112's rows: +0.0005 V (a bit-time peak; the LDO's
       input capacitance carries it; shown, not judged)

8. THE LINE FOR L4A-56
   CHANGE-METHOD: M-A as registered (a limiter ahead of the AP2112K at 184 C/W) has no window on printed limits: its 125 C current
   0.3056 A sits 7.7 % over normal service's own peak (S2 0.2839 A) and under row 7's (S3' 0.4240 A); serving them through limiting needs
   more capacitance than the latch-off limiter can start into and a latch timer neither maker prints. TAKE THE THERMAL-HEADROOM
   COMPANION (SESSION, W135-1): C1, TI TPS2553-1 (SLVS841F; DBV), RILIM 49.9 kOhm, IOS 0.470 to 0.570 A, latch-off after 5 to 10 ms,
   at each supervisor LDO's input, AND a regulator part in place of the AP2112K with, PRINTED: junction-to-ambient at most 98.6 C/W at
   the 14.0k corner, rated output and current limit at least 0.570 A, dropout at 0.570 A at most 0.240 V, input to at least 4.12 V.
   Second source: C2, Diodes AP22653A (DS41186), RLIM 49.9 kOhm, IOS 0.436 to 0.545 A, theta at most 103.3 C/W, latch after 2 to 20 ms
   WHY the companion and not K1: it keeps the drafted structure (pre-regulator, a private LDO a supervisor, CON-004's own branch) and
   its acceptance (T10-A2, T10-A3) and adds one SOT-23-6 and a resistor a supervisor; no served row is limited, so nothing rests on a
   timer's unprinted restart, the protocol or the firmware. K1 (a buck a supervisor, U25's AP63203) is the FALLBACK if no regulator
   with those printed figures fits board B's pockets: it was set aside for area and switching ripple on VDD and VDDA, not because it
   failed (T10 section 8). To reverse W135-1: take K1, or a limiter class that prints a band of +-3.7 % at 0.29 A (none of the four
   sheets read does)

9. THE PREDICATES
   T10-A3's printed figure reproduces from record l9t5's modules before the limiter's resistance replaces the sense           yes
   no candidate's band fits under the AP2112K's 125 C current with its minimum at row 7's peak (W1 closed at 184 C/W)         yes
   W2 at 184 C/W: a row-7 frame needs more bridging capacitance than the latch-off limiter starts into, for both candidates   yes
   both candidates print a fault timer (minimum and maximum) and a latch-off that only EN or power clears                     yes
   at 49.9 kOhm both candidates' minimum is over every served peak (S3') and no AP2112 package holds 125 C at their maximum   yes
   the limiter's resistance in place of the 0.3 ohm sense keeps T10-A3 at T10's own point                                     yes
   three companion limiters at their maximum stay inside U601's and the lead's printed ratings                                yes
   the AP2112's typical foldback is under every IOSmin, so the output short under the limit is excluded with a reason, not bounded yes

l4lim_screen: done
